    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "When you combine the Strategy and Chain of Responsibility patterns, something interesting happens: you get a highly flexible architecture that separates orthogonal concerns. The chain handles the \"what\" and \"when\" of processing-what needs to be done to the request and in what order. The strategies handle the \"how\"-how to accomplish a specific task once it's determined that task is needed. This separation means you can modify either dimension independently without touching the other."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
